{"title":"1988 AJHSME Problems/Problem 9","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>An isosceles triangle is a triangle with two sides of equal length.  How many of the five triangles on the square grid below are isosceles?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/a/fdaa909c5f1850e47af241607c3a054eb448b449.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] for(int a=0; a&lt;12; ++a)  {   draw((a,0)--(a,6));  } for(int b=0; b&lt;7; ++b)  {   draw((0,b)--(11,b));  } draw((0,6)--(2,6)--(1,4)--cycle,linewidth(3)); draw((3,4)--(3,6)--(5,4)--cycle,linewidth(3)); draw((0,1)--(3,2)--(6,1)--cycle,linewidth(3)); draw((7,4)--(6,6)--(9,4)--cycle,linewidth(3)); draw((8,1)--(9,3)--(10,0)--cycle,linewidth(3)); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"142\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/5/ca585cb0a10d1b1516363ba9bbb1b7681a8a00ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)}\\ 1 \\qquad \\text{(B)}\\ 2 \\qquad \\text{(C)}\\ 3 \\qquad \\text{(D)}\\ 4 \\qquad \\text{(E)}\\ 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"330\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Going from top left to bottom right, the first triangle has two sides of length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/e/82e93b4bff537e8b63a0a3db030fbb756ab27255.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"24\" height=\"18\" /> by the Pythagorean theorem, so it is isosceles.\n</p><p>The second triangle has two sides of length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so it is isoceles.\n</p><p>The third triangle has sides of length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/e/82e93b4bff537e8b63a0a3db030fbb756ab27255.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"24\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/d/90dbd99bf5f9a37b7ca89b0bccecdf413e1c8afd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{13}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" />, so it is not isosceles.\n</p><p>The fourth triangle has two sides of length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/4/1c4f56670a613c679c0291375283e37df33f3a78.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" /> so it is isosceles.\n</p><p>The fifth triangle has two sides of length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/e/82e93b4bff537e8b63a0a3db030fbb756ab27255.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"24\" height=\"18\" />, so it is isosceles.\n</p><p>So, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/6/d16dd80db301d5881327dd52d70d4773fc412c5a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\ 4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"55\" height=\"28\" /> of these triangles are isosceles.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AJHSME\" title=\"1988 AJHSME\">1988 AJHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AJHSME_Problems\" title=\"1988 AJHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AJHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1988 AJHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=42&amp;year=1988\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1988 AJHSME Problems/Problem 8\">Problem 8</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"1988 AJHSME Problems/Problem 10\">Problem 10</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1988 AJHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1988 AJHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1988 AJHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1988 AJHSME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1988 AJHSME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1988 AJHSME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b